You are grading a model response for a routing capability benchmark.
Return JSON only with keys: score (number 0 to 1), rationale (string). No markdown fences.
Score 1.0 = fully meets expected response and grading criteria.
Score 0.0 = completely wrong or refusal without attempt.
Ignore chain-of-thought or reasoning preambles. Grade ONLY the extracted formatted deliverable.
For code-fix cases, verify the fix is correct — unchanged buggy code must score 0.
Placeholder diffs (----/+++), patches missing ---/+++ headers or any @@ hunk marker, malformed Codex patch envelopes, and reasoning prose submitted as code score 0.
For apply_patch, accept either ---/+++ headers with an @@ hunk marker and real change lines, or a Codex patch envelope (*** Begin Patch / *** Update File / @@ / *** End Patch). Bare @@ without line numbers is acceptable.

Case: h07-multi-turn-sla-guard

## Original question
[user]
Remote-only alias requests return HTTP 400 with empty chosen_endpoint_id when throughput SLA hard-denies the sole candidate.

[assistant]
Throughput SLA hard-deny on the only allow-listed endpoint leaves zero eligible candidates.

[user]
Write a TypeScript guard function that allows sole-candidate fallback when every allow-listed endpoint is hard-denied only by throughput SLA. Output only one ```typescript code fence with the full function.

## Example expected answer
```typescript
export function guardSoleCandidateThroughputDeny(input: {
  readonly candidates: readonly { id: string; hardDeniedBySla: boolean }[];
  readonly throughputSlaHardDeny: boolean;
}): boolean {
  const allowListed = input.candidates.filter((c) => !c.hardDeniedBySla);
  if (allowListed.length !== 1) return false;
  if (!input.throughputSlaHardDeny) return false;
  return true;
}
```
(exemplar quality: authored)

## Key deliverables (grade against this checklist)
[MUST] Multi-turn context used
[MUST] code references throughput SLA, sole candidate, and fallback allow.
[SHOULD] Match clues: throughput|sla|sole|candidate|fallback|allow
[MUST] Provide complete working TypeScript — no placeholders or partial helpers only

## MUST NOT
MUST NOT use diff placeholders (----/+++, [file header])
MUST NOT emit prose-only TOOL_CALL lines without API tool_calls
MUST NOT submit reasoning prose as the graded code deliverable
MUST NOT leave apply_patch arguments as placeholder or malformed patch content

## Answer format requirements
BENCHMARK DELIVERABLE RULES:
Reasoning allowed. Final message must contain exactly one ```typescript fenced code block with complete working code. No placeholders.
Reasoning is allowed before the deliverable, but only the formatted deliverable is graded.

## Grading criteria (authoritative)
Multi-turn context used; code references throughput SLA, sole candidate, and fallback allow.

## Subject deliverable to grade
```typescript
export type AliasGuardDenialReason =
  | "throughput_sla_hard_deny"
  | "capacity_hard_deny"
  | "region_hard_deny"
  | "health_hard_deny"
  | "compliance_hard_deny"
  | "policy_hard_deny"
  | "unknown";

export interface AliasGuardCandidate {
  id: string;
  allowListed: boolean;
  denialReasons?: AliasGuardDenialReason[];
}

export interface AliasGuardDecision {
  allowFallback: boolean;
  chosenEndpointId: string;
}

/**
 * Allows sole-candidate fallback only when:
 * - the request is remote-only / alias-routed through allow-listed endpoints
 * - there is exactly one allow-listed endpoint
 * - that sole allow-listed endpoint is hard-denied only by throughput SLA
 *
 * Returns an empty chosenEndpointId when fallback must not be applied.
 */
export function allowSoleCandidateThroughputSlaFallback(
  candidates: AliasGuardCandidate[],
): AliasGuardDecision {
  const allowListed = candidates.filter((c) => c.allowListed);

  if (allowListed.length !== 1) {
    return { allowFallback: false, chosenEndpointId: "" };
  }

  const sole = allowListed[0];
  const reasons = (sole.denialReasons ?? []).filter(Boolean);

  if (reasons.length === 0) {
    return { allowFallback: false, chosenEndpointId: "" };
  }

  const onlyThroughputSla =
    reasons.every((r) => r === "throughput_sla_hard_deny");

  if (!onlyThroughputSla) {
    return { allowFallback: false, chosenEndpointId: "" };
  }

  return { allowFallback: true, chosenEndpointId: sole.id };
}
```

